   "Northwind-negotiator": "competing",
   "Halcyon-researcher": "collaborating",
   "Halcyon-drafter": "competing",
   "Halcyon-negotiator": "compromising"
  },
  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -1,
  "section_notes": "S2 sets a 5% benchmark but lets regulators decide on sales restrictions, with no automatic sales stop and no transition cap, and keeps per-model rates confidential from the public. S5 makes recall mandatory above 8 per 100,000, which the disclosed Ember 8 rate (9.9) exceeds, while S3 gives a 72-month retrofit window that favours Northwind's low installed shut-off coverage. S1 reporting is 24 hours for serious events only, with customer notice at 48 hours."
 },
